# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.

module super-accept "Super-accepting a Jacoby transfer"
  card   notrump.transfers.super_accept
  needs  jacoby-transfers
  skill  bidding_conventions/super_accept
  param  system = general.system   # `brill`: the Brill card's treatments

# Four-card support and 16-17 (2026-09-25: any four-card super-accept cost
# 1,517 IMPs to our side against 16+; see jacoby-transfers.notes.md): jump in
# the major. With superaccept-doubleton on as well,
# maximums with a doubleton choose the more descriptive doubleton bids, so
# this is left for maximums without one (4-3-3-3).
after nt1 2D (P) when system is not brill
  3H  "Super-accept: 4+ hearts, a maximum"   shows H>=4, hcp>=16
after nt1 2H (P) when system is not brill
  3S  "Super-accept: 4+ spades, a maximum"   shows S>=4, hcp>=16

# brill (the Brill card): the jump is the minimum with four trumps (a
# 4-3-3-3 minimum completes, jacoby-transfers.bid); maximums with four
# go through 2NT or the doubleton (superaccept-doubleton.bid). Brill
# /explain, 2026-10-15, "4+ hearts, min": `hearts > 3 and not max`;
# "4+ spades, min": `spades > 3 and not max`.
after nt1 2D (P) when system is brill
  3H  "Four or more hearts, a minimum"   shows H>=4, hcp<=15, shortest<=2
after nt1 2H (P) when system is brill
  3S  "Four or more spades, a minimum"   shows S>=4, hcp<=15, shortest<=2
